WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.810
- We've talked about
former President Trump's

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.230
ridiculous lawsuit against
a bunch of big tech firms

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.770
that de-platformed him,

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.630
and one of the arguments that he's making

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.300
is that these big tech firms

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.700
were deputized by the federal government

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.200
to effectively work as an arm
of the federal government.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.090
Now, that is something that can happen

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.010
if the federal government
contracts with a private company,

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.760
then sometimes that private company

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.380
can be an arm of the government,

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.490
but these are private companies

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:27.790
that haven't contracted
with the federal government

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.780
and they haven't been
deputized by the government.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.680
And, by the way, the government
that he's talking about,

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.640
given the timeframe, is the government

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.330
that he was running at the time,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.010
which is particularly ridiculous.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.820
But, as many people have pointed out,

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.490
this isn't so much a lawsuit
that has any chance of winning

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:46.470
so much as a fundraising effort
by Trump and his campaign.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.710
So, look, the metrics for
success are very different.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.910
So we're going to see Trump
in court for a little while,

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.360
but not for very much longer.

